{"id":"21-security","number":21,"slug":"prompt-injection-lethal-trifecta","title":"Security: prompt injection and the lethal trifecta","short":"Prompt injection and the lethal trifecta","module":"Quality, safety, teams","summary":"Agents follow instructions, including instructions hidden in web pages, issues and logs written by strangers. If an agent can also reach private data and send things out, an attacker can steal that data. Learn how prompt injection works, Simon Willison's lethal trifecta, why filters and prompt begging fail, and the defenses that actually work.","voice":"Eric","scenes":[{"template":"title","chapter":"Intro","narration":"If your agent can read your secrets, read things strangers wrote, and send data to the outside world, then someone else can control it. This might be the most important lesson in the course.","params":{"kicker":"Lesson 21","module":"Module 5 · Quality, safety, teams","title":"Security: prompt injection and the *lethal trifecta*","subtitle":"Why agents can be hijacked, and how to stop it.","bubble":"Wait, who said that?","mood":"alert"},"start":0.5,"dur":12.851,"words":[{"text":"If","s":0.8,"e":0.96},{"text":"your","s":1.04,"e":1.2},{"text":"agent","s":1.28,"e":1.52},{"text":"can","s":1.6,"e":1.76},{"text":"read","s":1.84,"e":2.08},{"text":"your","s":2.16,"e":2.24},{"text":"secrets,","s":2.32,"e":3.12},{"text":"read","s":3.2,"e":3.44},{"text":"things","s":3.6,"e":3.76},{"text":"strangers","s":3.88,"e":4.32},{"text":"wrote,","s":4.4,"e":4.96},{"text":"and","s":5.08,"e":5.2},{"text":"send","s":5.32,"e":5.44},{"text":"data","s":5.6,"e":5.76},{"text":"to","s":5.84,"e":5.88},{"text":"the","s":5.92,"e":6},{"text":"outside","s":6.2,"e":6.4},{"text":"world,","s":6.48,"e":7.2},{"text":"then","s":7.32,"e":7.44},{"text":"someone","s":7.52,"e":7.76},{"text":"else","s":7.84,"e":8.16},{"text":"can","s":8.24,"e":8.4},{"text":"control","s":8.6,"e":8.8},{"text":"it.","s":8.88,"e":9.52},{"text":"This","s":9.64,"e":9.76},{"text":"might","s":9.84,"e":9.92},{"text":"be","s":10,"e":10.08},{"text":"the","s":10.16,"e":10.32},{"text":"most","s":10.44,"e":10.56},{"text":"important","s":10.64,"e":11.12},{"text":"lesson","s":11.2,"e":11.52},{"text":"in","s":11.56,"e":11.6},{"text":"the","s":11.64,"e":11.68},{"text":"course.","s":11.76,"e":12.48}]},{"template":"quote","chapter":"Prompt injection","narration":"Simon Willison, who coined the term prompt injection, explains the root cause. Models can't reliably tell where an instruction came from. Your request, a web page, a GitHub issue: everything gets glued together into one sequence of tokens. So instructions hidden in content can hijack the agent.","params":{"text":"LLMs are unable to reliably distinguish the importance of instructions based on where they came from. Everything eventually gets *glued together* into a sequence of tokens.","who":"Simon Willison","role":"coined “prompt injection”","src":"The lethal trifecta for AI agents"},"start":13.351,"dur":20.437,"words":[{"text":"Simon","s":13.651,"e":14.051},{"text":"Willison,","s":14.131,"e":14.851},{"text":"who","s":14.931,"e":15.011},{"text":"coined","s":15.091,"e":15.331},{"text":"the","s":15.411,"e":15.491},{"text":"term","s":15.611,"e":15.731},{"text":"prompt","s":15.811,"e":16.051},{"text":"injection,","s":16.131,"e":16.851},{"text":"explains","s":16.931,"e":17.491},{"text":"the","s":17.531,"e":17.571},{"text":"root","s":17.651,"e":17.811},{"text":"cause.","s":17.891,"e":18.731},{"text":"Models","s":19.091,"e":19.491},{"text":"can't","s":19.571,"e":19.731},{"text":"reliably","s":19.811,"e":20.451},{"text":"tell","s":20.611,"e":20.771},{"text":"where","s":20.851,"e":20.931},{"text":"an","s":20.971,"e":21.011},{"text":"instruction","s":21.091,"e":21.651},{"text":"came","s":21.731,"e":21.971},{"text":"from.","s":22.051,"e":22.691},{"text":"Your","s":22.771,"e":22.851},{"text":"request,","s":23.171,"e":23.651},{"text":"a","s":23.731,"e":23.811},{"text":"web","s":23.931,"e":24.051},{"text":"page,","s":24.251,